# Next.js (`apps/api`)

This is **not** the Next.js from training data. APIs and conventions may differ.

## Before writing Next.js code

1. Read the relevant guide in `apps/api/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`
2. Heed deprecation notices in that docs tree
3. Mirror patterns in existing `apps/api/src/app/` files

## Project conventions

- **Build/dev use webpack:** `next dev --webpack`, `next build --webpack` (see `package.json`)
- **App Router:** routes in `apps/api/src/app/`
- **API routes:** `apps/api/src/app/api/` — protect cron/backup with `verifyApiSecret` from `@/lib/server/api-auth`
- **Client components:** `'use client'` only when needed (hooks, browser APIs, event handlers)
- **Env:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for client; secrets (`INTERNAL_API_SECRET`, `CRON_SECRET`) server-only
- **Surface:** API + book + portal + admin (+ legal). Operator PWA UI is removed — do not add it back.

## Do not assume

- Pages Router (`pages/`) — this app is App Router only
- Default Next 14/15 APIs without checking local docs
- `detailing-website/` has its own simpler setup — rules here target `apps/api/`

